{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8b9c6287-d7e2-4fd6-8dbd-dc6c5dce5337","agentId":"a8b24ce63139aab44","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: 1 search per fact, 5 checks, report under 100 words. Do not edit cuore/web/* or cuore/app.py. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; sources already in repo: mes-log-mcp/mes/knowledge.py (TSBs S1808000005 BCM feeds/F82, S2008000032 connectors XY201 and grounds G003A/B, S1708000262 terminals, 9100471 canister/ESIM, 9100325 hoses), docs/research/EVAP_STELVIO.md, docs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md, mes/systems.py (being written by another agent; read-only), mes/parts.py. House rules: every location/pin/connector id cites a source and confidence; UNKNOWN with \"use the service manual (TechAuthority) wiring diagrams\" where not sourced; never invent connector or pin numbers. Car: 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T.\n\nBuild:\n1. mes-log-mcp/mes/electrical.py: ELEMENTS keyed by id, kinds: fuse_box, fuse, relay, ground, connector, splice, harness_section, module, battery, alternator; each {kind, label, location: {zone: engine_bay|cabin_driver|cabin_passenger|dash|trunk|underbody|rear_left_wheel_well|..., description (plain words), source, confidence}, feeds: [element ids or module codes], part_of_systems: [systems keys], tsb_refs: [...], inspection_hint (what to look for: corrosion, chafe, backed-out pins, water ingress), notes}. Populate from the TSBs and docs above: battery (trunk? verify), BCM (location per module map), ECM, F82 and the BCM feed fuses, XY201 connector, G003A/G003B grounds, ESIM connector and its harness run (rear left wheel well area per EVAP docs), purge valve connector (engine bay), ABS/HALF, DASM radar, RFHUB, window-riser motor circuit (B1176) at a plain-words level. Mark UNKNOWN what you cannot source.\n2. CIRCUITS: per code (P0440/P0455/P0456/P0441/P1CEA, U0100/U1700-U1716/U1765/U1960/U2054/B1040 network family, B1176, C141B/C141C, P0300-04): ordered path [{element id, role: supply|protection|connector|component|ground|controller|bus}] with source/confidence per hop; code_electrical_path(code) -> {code, path: [...with element details inlined], systems_interaction: [{system, how: plain sentence, confidence, source}] (how each system interacts with this problem, e.g. EVAP: fuel system (tank/cap) + electrical (ESIM supply/ground) + ECM calibration; network: supply/grounds -> every module), inspect_steps: [{element id, what to check, how (voltage drop, wiggle test, visual), source}]}.\n3. Inspection records: JSONL <state>/electrical_inspections.jsonl rows {id, vin, element, at, by, condition: ok|corroded|chafed|loose|water|repaired|replaced|not_found, note, media_ids}; add/load/latest(vin, element). MCP tools: electrical_path(code), electrical_inspection_add(...), electrical_inspections(vin).\n4. cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py + cuore/api/electrical.py (GET /electrical/elements, /electrical/path/{code}, GET/POST /vehicles/{vin}/electrical/inspections); report include line.\n5. Tests (5): every element location has source or UNKNOWN; P0455 path includes a ground and the ESIM connector; network path starts at electrical supply (F82/BCM feeds); inspection add/latest round trip; API 200. Run + check_server.py."},"uuid":"8a292e25-af93-4a48-b1fe-b7fdd2878a18","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:44:02.082Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
