{"parentUuid":"e8454734-f736-4be3-9503-f153b985d9ea","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a8b24ce63139aab44","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp167Khdb4iCUsUP6bZK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RWhi3B2Snw61Dyfe5doiq3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"=== parts.py head ===\" && sed -n '1,60p' mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py && echo \"=== systems.py head ===\" && sed -n '1,80p' mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== find server file ===\" && grep -rl \"mcp.tool\\|@mcp\\.\" mes-log-mcp --include=*.py -l | head -20"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9791,"cache_read_input_tokens":72824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9791,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RWhi3B2Snw61Dyfe5doiq3":{"command":"cd /c/Users/User/mcp-servers && echo \"=== parts.py head ===\" && sed -n '1,60p' mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py && echo \"=== systems.py head ===\" && sed -n '1,80p' mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py 2>/dev/null && echo \"=== find server file ===\" && grep -rl \"mcp.tool\\|@mcp\\.\" mes-log-mcp --include=*.py -l | head -20"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01RWhi3B2Snw61Dyfe5doiq3":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b98f3c9-1dec-4bb4-890d-61e152803879","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfp16764kq5wiWhusNf7w","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad5b84d7-da38-4d04-a85c-390f56fe4e7b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:44:37.678Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"ad5b84d7-da38-4d04-a85c-390f56fe4e7b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8b9c6287-d7e2-4fd6-8dbd-dc6c5dce5337","agentId":"a8b24ce63139aab44","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 2\n=== parts.py head ===\n\"\"\"Reference data: parts for the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T (US).\n\nRead-only reference data -- nothing here touches the corpus or the car. It\nis the parts-catalogue counterpart to ``mes.service_specs`` (torques, oil/\nbrakes ledger) and ``mes.maintenance_specs`` (recurring maintenance items):\nthis module answers \"what part, what number, where, how much, where to buy\nit\" for a fixed set of commonly-needed parts, cross-linked to DTCs and to\nthe maintenance/service job keys that use them.\n\nConfidence levels (never invented -- an absent value is recorded as\nUNKNOWN, never guessed):\n\n* ``CONFIRMED``     -- an actual manufacturer document (owner's manual,\n                       Mopar/FCA parts catalog, FCA/Alfa TSB/service\n                       information, TechAuthority excerpt).\n* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent non-manufacturer sources agree.\n* ``SINGLE_SOURCE`` -- exactly one source found, not cross-checked.\n* ``UNKNOWN``       -- nothing credible found. ``number``/``price`` is\n                       ``None``, never a placeholder -- ``notes`` always\n                       points at the service manual.\n\nPart numbers are never invented. Where a Mopar catalog or VIN-fit listing\nwas not found, the number is left ``None`` with ``confidence=UNKNOWN`` and\na ``TECHAUTHORITY`` note. Images are link-only (never copied into this\nrepo) and, like ``buy`` links, are only included here after being checked\nto return HTTP 200 with a browser User-Agent during this research pass\n(2026-10-07) -- anything that failed that check was dropped rather than\nguessed at or left unverified.\n\nResearch sources for this pass: this repo's own ``docs/research/\nEVAP_STELVIO.md`` (which itself transcribes NHTSA-hosted FCA/Alfa TSBs --\n9100469 \"ESIM vs canister\" and 9100468 \"canister filter\"), the\n``mes.service_specs`` / ``mes.maintenance_specs`` / ``mes.drivetrain_specs``\nmodules already researched in this repo, the user's own repair-history memory\nfor this VIN (``project_stelvio_evap.md``), and RockAuto's part-number search\n(verified live, used only as a *buy* link, never as the source of a part\nnumber's identity).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nCONFIRMED = \"CONFIRMED\"\nCORROBORATED = \"CORROBORATED\"\nSINGLE_SOURCE = \"SINGLE-SOURCE\"\nUNKNOWN = \"UNKNOWN\"\n\nCONFIDENCE_LEVELS = (CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN)\n\nTECHAUTHORITY = \"use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"\n\nVEHICLE = (\"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T (GU), 2.0L GME-T4 MultiAir turbo, \"\n           \"sales code EC2, US market, Q4 AWD, ZF 8HP automatic\")\n\nFITS_VALUES = (\"stelvio_2.0t\", \"giorgio\", \"specific_vins\", \"grecale\", \"levante\")\n\n#: ``fits`` values treated as \"a sibling platform's car, not this one\" --\n#: see ``mes.platform``. No ``PARTS`` entry currently uses either value: a\n#: 2026-10-07 pass found no Grecale/Levante-specific, sourced part number\n=== systems.py head ===","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RWhi3B2Snw61Dyfe5doiq3"}]},"uuid":"6635abe6-dee8-410d-8662-6eccc045efcb","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:44:38.178Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 2\n=== parts.py head ===\n\"\"\"Reference data: parts for the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T (US).\n\nRead-only reference data -- nothing here touches the corpus or the car. It\nis the parts-catalogue counterpart to ``mes.service_specs`` (torques, oil/\nbrakes ledger) and ``mes.maintenance_specs`` (recurring maintenance items):\nthis module answers \"what part, what number, where, how much, where to buy\nit\" for a fixed set of commonly-needed parts, cross-linked to DTCs and to\nthe maintenance/service job keys that use them.\n\nConfidence levels (never invented -- an absent value is recorded as\nUNKNOWN, never guessed):\n\n* ``CONFIRMED``     -- an actual manufacturer document (owner's manual,\n                       Mopar/FCA parts catalog, FCA/Alfa TSB/service\n                       information, TechAuthority excerpt).\n* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent non-manufacturer sources agree.\n* ``SINGLE_SOURCE`` -- exactly one source found, not cross-checked.\n* ``UNKNOWN``       -- nothing credible found. ``number``/``price`` is\n                       ``None``, never a placeholder -- ``notes`` always\n                       points at the service manual.\n\nPart numbers are never invented. Where a Mopar catalog or VIN-fit listing\nwas not found, the number is left ``None`` with ``confidence=UNKNOWN`` and\na ``TECHAUTHORITY`` note. Images are link-only (never copied into this\nrepo) and, like ``buy`` links, are only included here after being checked\nto return HTTP 200 with a browser User-Agent during this research pass\n(2026-10-07) -- anything that failed that check was dropped rather than\nguessed at or left unverified.\n\nResearch sources for this pass: this repo's own ``docs/research/\nEVAP_STELVIO.md`` (which itself transcribes NHTSA-hosted FCA/Alfa TSBs --\n9100469 \"ESIM vs canister\" and 9100468 \"canister filter\"), the\n``mes.service_specs`` / ``mes.maintenance_specs`` / ``mes.drivetrain_specs``\nmodules already researched in this repo, the user's own repair-history memory\nfor this VIN (``project_stelvio_evap.md``), and RockAuto's part-number search\n(verified live, used only as a *buy* link, never as the source of a part\nnumber's identity).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nCONFIRMED = \"CONFIRMED\"\nCORROBORATED = \"CORROBORATED\"\nSINGLE_SOURCE = \"SINGLE-SOURCE\"\nUNKNOWN = \"UNKNOWN\"\n\nCONFIDENCE_LEVELS = (CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN)\n\nTECHAUTHORITY = \"use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"\n\nVEHICLE = (\"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T (GU), 2.0L GME-T4 MultiAir turbo, \"\n           \"sales code EC2, US market, Q4 AWD, ZF 8HP automatic\")\n\nFITS_VALUES = (\"stelvio_2.0t\", \"giorgio\", \"specific_vins\", \"grecale\", \"levante\")\n\n#: ``fits`` values treated as \"a sibling platform's car, not this one\" --\n#: see ``mes.platform``. No ``PARTS`` entry currently uses either value: a\n#: 2026-10-07 pass found no Grecale/Levante-specific, sourced part number\n=== systems.py head ===","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9b98f3c9-1dec-4bb4-890d-61e152803879","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"github","host":"github.com","remote":"dangelojohn/CUORE","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad5b84d7-da38-4d04-a85c-390f56fe4e7b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
